 "components": {
  "a": "Wilson 95 % lower bound vs n for k = 0, 1, 2, 5 errors; dashed lines at the pre-stated 90 % (exact level) and 85 % (variant sensitivity) targets; markers where each k clears each line; the k = 0 crossings labelled (35, 22).",
  "b": "Naming against training persons on one log axis (N = 0 at x = 2 left of a break). Film: exact-level naming on the v9 VAL films of the corpus against N training persons, render-only encoder fine-tuned per cell, seed mean with bars over the per-seed range (three seeds at N <= 25). C-arm: the v9 encoder and head fine-tuned per case-grouped fold on N C-ArmLSpine persons of one protocol and read on that protocol (lateral ink, anteroposterior grey, solid); the lateral-trained cells read on the anteroposterior test frames (ink dashed, open); the both-protocol cells at all persons (x). Reading: separated by view, each C-arm curve rises like film; the view not trained on stays where it was; training both views costs neither.",
  "c": "Same-device detection: vertebra recall (body boxes, confidence 0.74) on the 28 C-ArmLSpine test cases against N real frames of the device added to a fixed background, both views of N/2 patients, read on the lateral (ink) and anteroposterior (grey) test frames with case-clustered intervals; one-view arms of 25 and 50 frames of one protocol read on it (filled triangles) and on the other (open triangles), two seeds pooled. Reading: the plateau from 24 frames is the same pooled or separated; frames of one view buy that view and not the other.",
  "d": "Render-only detectors of the Surgio-B51 card at matched N (2,646 renders of 125 subjects) whose training poses are the real anteroposterior-lateral pool (vermillion), an arc (blue) or the real pool doubled (green), read at confidence 0.25 on 40 unseen subjects' renders per lateral angle (tilt 0); seed mean, per-seed range shaded; dotted verticals at the three trained angles. Reading: accuracy sits where the training poses sit; doubling the same poses raises those bins and not the gaps; the same N spread over the arc holds at every angle."
 },
