 "discrepancies_stated": [
  "Panel (b) mixes evaluation sets: film cells are scored on the corpus's fixed VAL films (persons never in any cell's training), C-arm cells on five case-grouped test folds pooled (148 lateral / 149 anteroposterior cases; 623 / 633 vertebrae); a C-ArmLSpine case is an acquisition session, counted as a person. The C-arm N = 0 cell is the fine-tune recipe with no C-arm crop; the zero-shot run (no C-arm image at all: lateral 96.3 %, anteroposterior 43.9 %) is in power.json and not drawn.",
  "Panel (b) draws no C-arm interval (the per-point case-clustered intervals are in power.json and the record; at N <= 25 three seeds are averaged, above one seed). The anteroposterior-trained cells read on the lateral test frames (93.4-95.3 %, not drawn) sit on the lateral own-view curve.",
  "Panel (c): under the body rule the N = 0 floor (lateral 0.2 %, anteroposterior 15.2 %) is a box-convention artefact (det_fill.json 'reading'): arms without C-ArmLSpine frames draw whole-vertebra boxes, which the body rule scores as misses; the convention-free centre rule reads 70.5 % at N = 0. The curve from N = 4 upward is unaffected in shape.",
  "Panel (c): the one-view arms at 25 frames use the same patients as the both-view arm at 50 frames and the same frame count as the both-view arm at 24; at 50 frames, the patients of the both-view 100 and the frame count of the both-view 50. Paired contrasts against both are in det_fill.json#contrasts.",
  "Panel (d): the Surgio card renders thick laterals photon-starved (recall_vs_angle.md), so the +-90 degree bins conflate geometry with synthetic underexposure; the +-30 to 60 degree bins carry the comparison. Every subject is placed on one anchor, so another subject's truth boxes already score about 0.64-0.68 at every angle (supplement); the bins are read against that floor, not zero.",
  "Panel (d) is renders at confidence 0.25 (the operating point every arm evaluator reports at), not the manuscript's detectors at 0.74; every render-only arm scores under 15 % on any real test set. The six Elekta XVI arms did not train (val mAP50 0.13-0.22) and are not drawn.",
  "The pooled nested fit (delta AICc 26.0, g +20.0 points per unit H*; at confidence 0.74 g -0.7, delta AICc -3.1; trained-only g +24.2) is quoted in Results and no longer drawn; g is identified by the Surgio arms alone.",
  "Film asymptotes: NHANES II and BUU-LSPINE are still rising at N = all (3.2 and 3.1 points below their fitted asymptotes); only CSXA plateaus (within 2 points from N = 200). The film cross-corpus transfer (dashed in the 10:26 build) is quoted in Results and no longer drawn."
 ],
 "reading": "At zero errors, 35 transitional persons put the Wilson lower bound at 90 % and 22 at 85 %. Film: NHANES II 77.8 % at N = 5 and 92.7 % at all 264; BUU-LSPINE 65.0 -> 96.9 % (2967); CSXA 94.2 -> 99.8 % (4114). C-arm naming: lateral 93.7 % at N = 0 -> 98.1 % at 50; anteroposterior 33.8 -> 90.8 % at 5 -> 98.1 % at all; lateral-trained on anteroposterior 54.7 % at all; both views 98.1 / 97.0 %. Detection (body, 0.74): both-view arm lateral 84.1 / anteroposterior 84.6 % at 24 frames, 81.2 / 84.6 % at 200; one-view arms 83.0-86.4 % on their own view, 0.0-39.5 % on the other. Angle (renders, 0.25): low arm 82.1 % at the trained angles and 52.8 % over the 16 others; 2N 94.2 / 64.8 %; arc 80.7 / 77.1 %."
}